      "content": "Neonatal jaundice: ~60% of full-term newborns develop it in the first week. Fetal red blood cells ma\n\nNeonatal jaundice: ~60% of full-term newborns develop it in the first week. Fetal red blood cells mass-breakdown at birth floods bilirubin faster than the immature liver can clear. Phototherapy (blue light) breaks bilirubin through the skin. Untreated severe cases = kernicterus (permanent brain damage). Treatment threshold varies with gestational age. #babyfacts #neonataljaundice #newborn #infantscience",
