      "content": "Newborns flood their bodies with catecholamines at birth — exceeding levels in adults during heart a\n\nNewborns flood their bodies with catecholamines at birth — exceeding levels in adults during heart attacks. It clears amniotic fluid from lungs, closes fetal vascular shunts, activates brown fat thermogenesis, switches circulation. C-section without labor blunts this surge — 3x higher wet lung rate. The stress of birth is physiologically necessary. #babyfacts #birthscience #catecholamines #birthbiology",
